00:11:06,394 --> 00:11:10,404
(Everyone is busy slurping.)

253
00:11:11,034 --> 00:11:12,104
(In love with the napa cabbage soup)

254
00:11:12,104 --> 00:11:13,164
It's really good.

255
00:11:13,164 --> 00:11:14,434
- Is it really good?
- Yes.

256
00:11:17,504 --> 00:11:18,674
It's amazing.

257
00:11:20,244 --> 00:11:22,174
- Shall I try some?
- It's really good.

258
00:11:22,314 --> 00:11:23,584
- Right.
- It's a work of art.

259
00:11:25,244 --> 00:11:27,014
(Taking one more bite)

260
00:11:27,654 --> 00:11:29,584
(My dish is delicious.)

261
00:11:30,114 --> 00:11:33,824
(The refreshing broth goes perfectly with the grilled wild eel.)

262
00:11:34,294 --> 00:11:38,124
(After cleansing her palate, she focuses on the wild eel again.)

263
00:11:38,594 --> 00:11:42,364
(The wild eel is healthy and tasty.)

264
00:11:43,234 --> 00:11:47,034
(The long, exhausting day’s fatigue)

265
00:11:47,974 --> 00:11:52,904
(It's wiped away in one shot by this ultimate stamina food.)

266
00:11:53,674 --> 00:11:56,574
(There's another person who's hooked on wild eel.)

267
00:11:57,084 --> 00:11:58,814
(He's eating,)

268
00:11:58,814 --> 00:12:01,514
(eating,)

269
00:12:01,514 --> 00:12:05,524
(and eating again.)

270
00:12:05,524 --> 00:12:08,794
Honestly, I've never been a huge fan of eel.

271
00:12:08,794 --> 00:12:10,324
- You don't like eels that much?
- No.

272
00:12:10,324 --> 00:12:11,564
(But he's getting ready for one more bite.)

273
00:12:11,694 --> 00:12:14,394
Wild eel grilled over charcoal is...

274
00:12:14,394 --> 00:12:16,064
- very rare.
- It's so delicious.

275
00:12:16,494 --> 00:12:18,864
It's my first time eating this much eel.

276
00:12:19,364 --> 00:12:21,204
It's because it's not greasy. You can't stop eating it.

277
00:12:21,204 --> 00:12:22,804
- It's not greasy at all.
- You keep reaching for more.

278
00:12:23,574 --> 00:12:26,604
I can still remember the feeling of catching those eels.

279
00:12:27,974 --> 00:12:31,084
(Come on, eel. Get in my mouth.)

280
00:12:31,814 --> 00:12:33,014
That's why we worked hard to catch them.

281
00:12:33,014 --> 00:12:36,114
(Everyone is thoroughly enjoying the wild eel feast.)

282
00:12:36,554 --> 00:12:37,754
Gosh, my yakbab.

283
00:12:38,524 --> 00:12:40,394
What's the matter, Jung Ah?

284
00:12:40,594 --> 00:12:42,024
I'll go and take a look.

285
00:12:42,024 --> 00:12:43,224
(She ends up heading over to the yakbab.)

286
00:12:43,864 --> 00:12:47,394
(Has the huge batch of yakbab turned out well?)

287
00:12:47,834 --> 00:12:50,704
(Steam rising)

288
00:12:51,364 --> 00:12:53,934
(It looks well cooked, moist and glistening.)

289
00:12:54,804 --> 00:12:57,904
(Here comes a giant spatula to stir 40 servings all at once.)

290
00:12:59,244 --> 00:13:04,984
(Thick and sticky)

291
00:13:05,444 --> 00:13:08,254
(A drizzle of sesame oil for extra nuttiness)

292
00:13:08,814 --> 00:13:11,854
(Another powerful round of stirring to mix everything evenly)

293
00:13:12,454 --> 00:13:15,954
(This yakbab is for the younger siblings to taste.)

294
00:13:15,954 --> 00:13:16,994
It looks delicious.

295
00:13:17,294 --> 00:13:19,594
I'll check and see if it's cooked.

296
00:13:20,094 --> 00:13:21,734
- All of it is cooked.
- Now...

297
00:13:21,734 --> 00:13:23,334
- Is it cooked?
- It's cooked.

298
00:13:23,334 --> 00:13:25,664
(Hot yakbab goes straight into her mouth.)

299
00:13:25,664 --> 00:13:26,834
Isn't it a little bland?

300
00:13:26,834 --> 00:13:28,374
- It's very bland.
- I know.

301
00:13:29,174 --> 00:13:32,004
I didn't know the exact amount,

302
00:13:32,004 --> 00:13:33,844
so I didn't get the portions right.

303
00:13:34,714 --> 00:13:36,014
It'll taste sweeter once it cools down.

304
00:13:36,014 --> 00:13:37,344
- Really?
- Yes.

305
00:13:38,544 --> 00:13:41,584
(With all her strength)

306
00:13:42,054 --> 00:13:44,584
(The cooked yakbab is transferred into a container.)

307
00:13:44,924 --> 00:13:47,554
(Press it down and shape it even)

308
00:13:47,754 --> 00:13:50,124
This is made with love.

309
00:13:50,124 --> 00:13:51,424
(After sprinkling savory pine nuts)

310
00:13:51,824 --> 00:13:53,324
Once I shape it like this,

311
00:13:53,594 --> 00:13:55,894
- I let it cool...
- Okay.

312
00:13:55,894 --> 00:13:57,034
and slice it later.

313
00:13:57,604 --> 00:13:59,304
Does it taste good? Did it turn out well?

314
00:13:59,304 --> 00:14:00,374
It's very bland.

315
00:14:00,804 --> 00:14:01,834
Then we'll just eat it.

316
00:14:01,834 --> 00:14:03,604
Instead of giving it to them in person,

317
00:14:03,604 --> 00:14:05,004
let's leave it behind with a letter.

318
00:14:06,574 --> 00:14:09,874
(That's original.)

319
00:14:09,944 --> 00:14:12,144
- Let the gesture speak for itself?
- A handwritten letter with love.

320
00:14:13,014 --> 00:14:14,254
- Jung Ah, it tastes good.
- What?

321
00:14:14,254 --> 00:14:16,714
- Does it taste okay?
- It's very good.

322
00:14:16,714 --> 00:14:17,724
(Please turn out delicious)

323
00:14:18,384 --> 00:14:19,624
What time are we getting up tomorrow?

324
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:22,154
Actually, I have an announcement to make.

325
00:14:22,154 --> 00:14:23,624
It must be a major announcement.

326
00:14:23,624 --> 00:14:25,024
Someone is going to the green tea fields.

327
00:14:25,024 --> 00:14:26,194
- Oh, my gosh.
- Who will it be?

328
00:14:26,194 --> 00:14:29,994
You're in Hadong and Gwangyang right now.

329
00:14:30,164 --> 00:14:32,604
They're Korea's biggest green plum growing regions.

330
00:14:32,604 --> 00:14:33,834
- Green plums?
- I see.

331
00:14:34,334 --> 00:14:37,574
Tomorrow, you're going green plum harvesting.

332
00:14:38,144 --> 00:14:39,304
Unfortunately,

333
00:14:39,704 --> 00:14:42,114
- only three people can go.
- That's so unfortunate.

334
00:14:42,114 --> 00:14:43,414
I really wanted to go.

335
00:14:43,414 --> 00:14:44,814
That's such a shame.

336
00:14:44,814 --> 00:14:45,944
(Gosh, it's such a shame.)

337
00:14:46,144 --> 00:14:47,854
That's a shame. I wanted to go.

338
00:14:47,854 --> 00:14:49,454
Have fun, Yoon Seo.

339
00:14:49,784 --> 00:14:51,824
- Gosh, it's going to make me cry.
- Have fun, Yoon Seo.

340
00:14:51,824 --> 00:14:53,754
Picking green plums is seriously on my bucket list.

341
00:14:54,254 --> 00:14:56,894
(As long as it's not me)

342
00:14:56,894 --> 00:14:58,024
I won't let this slide.

343
00:14:58,024 --> 00:14:59,764
(If I get picked again, I'll be angry at myself.)

344
00:15:00,294 --> 00:15:01,564
Did you see my legs?

345
00:15:01,934 --> 00:15:03,094
I can't even sit down.

346
00:15:03,594 --> 00:15:05,034
I can't sit down or stand properly.

347
00:15:05,464 --> 00:15:07,604
I'm completely worn out.

348
00:15:08,104 --> 00:15:09,704
I've been to every work assignment.

349
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:13,004
- Let's vote...
- You Seok worked the least.

350
00:15:13,004 --> 00:15:14,474
Jin Hee, what do you think?

351
00:15:15,844 --> 00:15:17,044
What do you want to do?

352
00:15:17,544 --> 00:15:18,684
Tell us what you think.

353
00:15:19,584 --> 00:15:20,584
Jin Hee...

354
00:15:20,584 --> 00:15:21,614
Does he have to list the reasons why he shouldn't go?

355
00:15:21,614 --> 00:15:23,314
Why are you just wiping the table quietly?

356
00:15:23,314 --> 00:15:24,984
- I mean...
- Bring it in.

357
00:15:25,254 --> 00:15:26,984
It's a very simple game.

358
00:15:29,394 --> 00:15:31,024
- Seriously?
- What's that?

359
00:15:31,564 --> 00:15:32,794
It's Americano and...

360
00:15:32,794 --> 00:15:34,194
(Mysterious drinks appear.)

361
00:15:34,494 --> 00:15:36,664
I never imagined that I'd be doing this.

362
00:15:36,964 --> 00:15:40,474
(5 drinks are prepared to select 3 people for green plum picking.)

363
00:15:40,904 --> 00:15:45,044
(2 green plum syrup ades and 3 sand lance sauce drinks)

364
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:47,244
(Only three people to pick sand lance sauce...)

365
00:15:47,244 --> 00:15:49,014
(go green plum picking.)

366
00:15:49,614 --> 00:15:52,684
(Who will be the lucky ones to meet the green plums of Gwangyang?)

367
00:15:53,244 --> 00:15:54,714
- What is it?
- It's sand lance sauce.

368
00:15:54,714 --> 00:15:55,754
Go ahead and pick first.

369
00:15:55,754 --> 00:15:57,154
They look exactly the same.

370
00:15:57,984 --> 00:15:58,984
This is fun.

371
00:15:59,554 --> 00:16:01,954
- Don't look.
- You have to look.

372
00:16:02,554 --> 00:16:04,494
I've been to every work assignment.

373
00:16:04,594 --> 00:16:05,994
He didn't work even once.

374
00:16:06,464 --> 00:16:08,334
- It's impossible to tell.
- Can we line up...

375
00:16:08,334 --> 00:16:10,734
(They even resort to using their sense of smell.)

376
00:16:10,964 --> 00:16:12,804
(Meanwhile, Sun Young keeps a close eye on the cups.)

377
00:16:12,834 --> 00:16:14,474
Now I know.

378
00:16:14,734 --> 00:16:16,374
(Do you really...)

379
00:16:16,374 --> 00:16:17,444
- You know?
- Yes.

380
00:16:17,704 --> 00:16:20,944
Two of them are clearly Americano.

381
00:16:20,944 --> 00:16:22,574
- There's no Americano.
- There's no Americano.

382
00:16:23,344 --> 00:16:24,944
- There's no Americano.
- There's no Americano, Sun Young.

383
00:16:24,944 --> 00:16:27,154
Two of them are clearly green plum syrup.

384
00:16:27,154 --> 00:16:28,414
Three of them are sand lance sauce.

385
00:16:28,414 --> 00:16:29,784
- You should pick first.
- Okay.

386
00:16:29,914 --> 00:16:32,524
I don't mind being called a braggart,

387
00:16:32,524 --> 00:16:33,794
so I'll tell you the answer.

388
00:16:33,924 --> 00:16:35,194
- Tell us.
- Let's hear it, Sun Young.

389
00:16:35,894 --> 00:16:38,064
- Number 1.
- Is this number 1?

390
00:16:38,064 --> 00:16:39,364
And number four.

391
00:16:40,694 --> 00:16:42,334
This is number one, and it goes in this order.

392
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:43,964
- In this order?
- Yes.

393
00:16:44,904 --> 00:16:45,934
What's the reason?

394
00:16:46,204 --> 00:16:47,634
- Just because.
- Just because?

395
00:16:47,634 --> 00:16:48,704
It's based on my feelings.

396
00:16:48,734 --> 00:16:49,734
- Your feelings?
- Yes.

397
00:16:49,734 --> 00:16:52,044
- I don't see the color difference.
- You have ten seconds.

398
00:16:53,204 --> 00:16:55,444
(Concentrating)

399
00:16:55,444 --> 00:16:57,814
(Being careful)

400
00:16:57,814 --> 00:16:59,884
(Scanning)

401
00:16:59,944 --> 00:17:01,054
I pick number five.

402
00:17:01,484 --> 00:17:03,514
(Picking number five, which was Sun Young's choice)

403
00:17:03,514 --> 00:17:05,024
- I pick number 2.
- I pick number 4.

404
00:17:05,654 --> 00:17:06,754
Number one.

405
00:17:06,984 --> 00:17:08,194
(Jung Ah who can't decide)

406
00:17:08,194 --> 00:17:09,894
- Yours is number three.
- I'll take what's left.

407
00:17:10,054 --> 00:17:11,194
I have no idea.

408
00:17:11,194 --> 00:17:14,164
(Everyone made their choice.)

409
00:17:14,334 --> 00:17:15,564
I'm really scared.

410
00:17:17,364 --> 00:17:21,434
(Yoon Seo who has been picked for every labor)

411
00:17:21,434 --> 00:17:25,404
(Yum Jung Ah and Roh Yoon Seo, please get up now.)

412
00:17:26,304 --> 00:17:32,644
(You Seok avoided labor for the last 3 days.)

413
00:17:33,284 --> 00:17:34,954
(Determined)

414
00:17:35,354 --> 00:17:37,684
(Sun Young's record: 1 time, onion harvesting)

415
00:17:38,184 --> 00:17:40,594
(Jung Ah's record, 1 time at poultry farm)

416
00:17:40,854 --> 00:17:42,124
(The next workers will be decided purely by luck.)

417
00:17:42,124 --> 00:17:43,254
Let's go.

418
00:17:43,724 --> 00:17:44,964
The color looks strange.

419
00:17:45,394 --> 00:17:47,124
It's red and dark.

420
00:17:47,394 --> 00:17:49,064
(Checking the color one more time)

421
00:17:49,064 --> 00:17:50,234
- Simultaneously...
- Does no one know...

422
00:17:50,234 --> 00:17:51,434
- which one is which?
- I don't know either.

423
00:17:51,664 --> 00:17:52,664
Shall we drink it?

424
00:17:53,204 --> 00:17:54,274
Let's go.

425
00:17:54,774 --> 00:17:56,734
- Okay.
- In the count of three,

426
00:17:56,734 --> 00:17:57,944
- drink it up.
- Without stopping.

427
00:17:57,944 --> 00:17:58,974
Take a big sip?

428
00:18:00,944 --> 00:18:01,944
One.

429
00:18:04,144 --> 00:18:05,144
Two.

430
00:18:07,814 --> 00:18:08,884
Three.

431
00:18:09,314 --> 00:18:10,854
(Drinking)

432
00:18:11,084 --> 00:18:12,624
(Eyes tightly shut)

433
00:18:12,854 --> 00:18:16,524
(Unidentified drinks are gulped down simultaneously.)

434
00:18:20,594 --> 00:18:22,364
(Spitting out sand lance sauce)

435
00:18:23,464 --> 00:18:25,964
(Meanwhile, she moves to minimize the damage.)

436
00:18:26,264 --> 00:18:28,974
(Jung Ah is the first one picked for labor.)

437
00:18:29,374 --> 00:18:32,444
(Is everyone else fine?)

438
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:35,174
(Of course not)

439
00:18:36,574 --> 00:18:38,544
(Tilting his head)

440
00:18:38,544 --> 00:18:39,544
(Gasping)

441
00:18:39,544 --> 00:18:41,414
(The smell of sand lance sauce hits a beat later.)

442
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:44,754
(You Seok is picked for labor for the 1st time in 3 days.)

443
00:18:45,824 --> 00:18:49,424
(The intense, umami flavor is hard to shake off.)

444
00:18:49,894 --> 00:18:52,964
(Two workers are chosen.)

445
00:18:53,664 --> 00:18:54,864
I can't drink this.

446
00:18:58,434 --> 00:19:00,534
Is it the three of us?

447
00:19:00,934 --> 00:19:02,304
No, I'm touched.

448
00:19:03,974 --> 00:19:05,044
Who is it?

449
00:19:05,044 --> 00:19:06,244
(There are only 2 cups of green plum syrup.)

450
00:19:06,704 --> 00:19:07,774
Sun Young is holding it in.

451
00:19:09,214 --> 00:19:10,614
Are you holding it in?

452
00:19:10,614 --> 00:19:12,514
(Is either Sun Young or Jin Hee holding in the strong flavor?)

453
00:19:12,514 --> 00:19:13,884
Jin Hee is holding it in.

454
00:19:14,884 --> 00:19:16,384
But it's way too strong.

455
00:19:16,384 --> 00:19:17,484
(Can he really hold it in?)

456
00:19:17,754 --> 00:19:19,584
- Are you crying?
- But it's way too strong.

457
00:19:19,884 --> 00:19:20,894
(However...)

458
00:19:20,894 --> 00:19:22,654
The green plum syrup isn't very good.

459
00:19:23,454 --> 00:19:25,264
Yoon Seo, I asked you to switch with mine.

460
00:19:25,624 --> 00:19:27,534
Try it. It's not good either.

461
00:19:27,534 --> 00:19:28,594
(You Seok grabs Yoon Seo's green plum syrup.)

462
00:19:31,964 --> 00:19:34,434
Yours is sand lance sauce.

463
00:19:34,574 --> 00:19:35,974
Is this sand lance sauce?

464
00:19:36,934 --> 00:19:38,444
Two of them got green plum syrup.

465
00:19:38,444 --> 00:19:40,244
Yours is sand lance sauce.

466
00:19:40,874 --> 00:19:42,074
Is this sand lance sauce?

467
00:19:42,444 --> 00:19:43,674
It tastes similar to green plum syrup.

468
00:19:43,674 --> 00:19:45,414
Can I take a sip of green plum syrup?

469
00:19:45,544 --> 00:19:47,984
Did you think sand lance sauce was green plum syrup?

470
00:19:48,154 --> 00:19:50,514
How could you not tell the difference?

471
00:19:50,514 --> 00:19:52,454
- Is yours green plum?
- Number one was good.

472
00:19:54,324 --> 00:19:55,894
Suddenly, I feel sick.

473
00:19:56,494 --> 00:19:57,794
It hits you late.

474
00:19:57,794 --> 00:19:59,524
She looked so sure of herself.

475
00:19:59,524 --> 00:20:00,734
(She gets picked for labor 3 times in a row.)

476
00:20:00,734 --> 00:20:02,334
I thought number one was...

477
00:20:02,594 --> 00:20:04,704
Sun Young, you said that it was number 2 and 5.

478
00:20:05,464 --> 00:20:08,604
(Sorry about that)

479
00:20:09,004 --> 00:20:12,904
Jung Ah, You Seok, and Yoon Seo will work tomorrow.

480
00:20:12,904 --> 00:20:14,414
Don't you think this is wrong?

481
00:20:14,414 --> 00:20:15,644
(She gets chosen for work 3 times in a row.)

482
00:20:15,644 --> 00:20:16,814
Let's be honest.

483
00:20:16,974 --> 00:20:18,544
I don't think this is right.

484
00:20:19,214 --> 00:20:21,514
Yoon Seo always has work coming her way.

485
00:20:21,514 --> 00:20:23,254
I guess I'm destined to work.

486
00:20:23,914 --> 00:20:26,554
- No, I'm just unlucky.
- You'll work again next time.

487
00:20:27,024 --> 00:20:29,554
Yoon Seo will work until the very end.

488
00:20:29,924 --> 00:20:31,824
You shouldn't say things like that.

489
00:20:32,494 --> 00:20:34,794
She's never skipped work.

490
00:20:35,294 --> 00:20:36,694
Our dear Yoon Seo.

491
00:20:36,694 --> 00:20:37,834
(2 people on house duty, 3 people for green plum harvesting)

492
00:20:37,834 --> 00:20:39,104
I should work since I'm the youngest.

493
00:20:39,564 --> 00:20:42,904
- Jin Hee and I go grocery shopping?
- We'll go grocery shopping.

494
00:20:43,374 --> 00:20:46,974
We need to discuss briefly about serving 40 people tomorrow.

495
00:20:47,344 --> 00:20:48,844
After that, we'll go grocery shopping.

496
00:20:49,574 --> 00:20:53,514
We need to go over this.

497
00:20:53,514 --> 00:20:55,054
When should we go grocery shopping?

498
00:20:55,054 --> 00:20:56,654
You should handle it yourself now.

499
00:20:56,654 --> 00:20:57,784
- Me?
- Yes.

500
00:20:58,254 --> 00:21:00,454
I feel overwhelmed.

501
00:21:01,224 --> 00:21:02,554
She's going to pick green plums,

502
00:21:02,554 --> 00:21:03,694
- so she'll be busy.
- So...

503
00:21:03,924 --> 00:21:05,564
Braised ribs and...

504
00:21:05,564 --> 00:21:06,794
Are we going to make braised ribs?

505
00:21:06,924 --> 00:21:08,834
- Braised pork ribs.
- Braised ribs and pasta.

506
00:21:09,634 --> 00:21:10,764
And seaweed soup.

507
00:21:10,904 --> 00:21:12,464
We're going to make seaweed soup with beef,

508
00:21:12,464 --> 00:21:13,864
so you need to buy some beef too.

509
00:21:16,304 --> 00:21:17,444
Okay, Sun Young?

510
00:21:18,104 --> 00:21:20,004
- Or Sun Young...
- I think we should...

511
00:21:20,144 --> 00:21:21,274
Let's play the game again.

512
00:21:21,814 --> 00:21:23,814
- I want to work with them.
- Why? You...

513
00:21:24,144 --> 00:21:26,244
Grocery shopping without Jung Ah just won't work.

514
00:21:26,684 --> 00:21:28,584
- Because she's our head chef...
- That's not true.

515
00:21:29,784 --> 00:21:31,324
- You just have to buy what we need.
- I can't pick the right things.

516
00:21:31,324 --> 00:21:32,324
I can't pick the right things, Jung Ah.

517
00:21:32,324 --> 00:21:35,024
What's with grocery shopping? It's not so hard.

518
00:21:35,254 --> 00:21:36,724
Are you a good cook?

519
00:21:36,724 --> 00:21:38,464
We're talking about grocery shopping, not cooking.

520
00:21:39,194 --> 00:21:41,364
Sun Young, it's for 40 people.

521
00:21:41,764 --> 00:21:43,394
Are we going to make 40 servings of braised ribs?

522
00:21:43,394 --> 00:21:44,434
- Yes.
- Yes.

523
00:21:45,134 --> 00:21:47,504
But braised ribs... That dish...

524
00:21:47,504 --> 00:21:48,934
Should we use bone-in ribs?

525
00:21:48,934 --> 00:21:51,474
I'll just ask the butcher to prep the ribs.

526
00:21:51,704 --> 00:21:53,774
- Prepping the ribs...
- They prep the ribs for you.

527
00:21:53,774 --> 00:21:55,614
- I mean, they cut the ribs for you.
- Right. They cut the meat.

528
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:57,114
- Should we just score the meat?
- So...

529
00:21:57,114 --> 00:22:00,244
We have to boil the meat first and then score it...

530
00:22:00,244 --> 00:22:02,084
We have to get pre-cut frozen meat, right?

531
00:22:02,084 --> 00:22:03,954
- You shouldn't get frozen meat.
- We shouldn't?

532
00:22:04,054 --> 00:22:05,224
You should get fresh meat.

533
00:22:05,224 --> 00:22:06,424
- Oh, okay.
- You can just tell the butcher...

534
00:22:06,424 --> 00:22:07,954
- that it's for braised pork ribs.
- Right.

535
00:22:07,954 --> 00:22:11,294
That's at least one piece of meat per person...

536
00:22:11,294 --> 00:22:13,194
No, wait. Each person will have...

537
00:22:13,424 --> 00:22:15,364
- at least two pieces, right?
- Yes.

538
00:22:15,364 --> 00:22:17,094
It has to be at least three pieces per person.

539
00:22:17,094 --> 00:22:18,334
They won't be able to eat that much...

540
00:22:18,334 --> 00:22:20,534
- as they'll have rice and soup too.
- They'll eat at least five pieces.

541
00:22:20,664 --> 00:22:23,234
No, three pieces are the minimum for the elderly.

542
00:22:25,144 --> 00:22:27,644
Prepping the meat will be no joke.

543
00:22:29,244 --> 00:22:30,744
(Buying ribs for 40 people)

544
00:22:30,744 --> 00:22:32,244
(Prepping the meat)

545
00:22:32,244 --> 00:22:33,714
(Cutting and washing)

546
00:22:33,914 --> 00:22:37,214
(It's so important for us to treat the villagers to a proper meal.)

547
00:22:37,384 --> 00:22:39,324
- Jung Ah, I want to go.
- Yes?

548
00:22:39,324 --> 00:22:40,484
- No, that's okay.
- But Jung Ah,

549
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:42,194
- your back hurts.
- It's been decided. That's okay.

550
00:22:42,494 --> 00:22:44,624
Prepping the ingredients will take a really long time.

551
00:22:44,624 --> 00:22:46,924
- That's true.
- Three hours won't cut it.

552
00:22:47,394 --> 00:22:49,294
- Potatoes and such.
- Yes, chopping them will help.

553
00:22:49,294 --> 00:22:51,334
Exactly. We should chop them so you can use them.

554
00:22:51,334 --> 00:22:53,564
We should wash everything before you come back.

555
00:22:53,564 --> 00:22:54,804
Then we'll have to leave right away,

556
00:22:54,804 --> 00:22:56,034
- but we don't have enough time.
- Right.

557
00:22:59,744 --> 00:23:01,814
Then count me out of picking green plums.

558
00:23:02,174 --> 00:23:03,414
I think I should stay here to shop for the ingredients...

559
00:23:03,414 --> 00:23:04,944
and prep them.

560
00:23:05,144 --> 00:23:07,584
Only then can we save some time for cooking.

561
00:23:08,614 --> 00:23:10,884
It's important to treat the seniors to a proper meal...

562
00:23:10,884 --> 00:23:12,124
as well as to pick green plums.

563
00:23:12,124 --> 00:23:13,524
- I'll go instead of Jung Ah.
- All right.

564
00:23:13,754 --> 00:23:15,254
Right. I'll go.

565
00:23:15,524 --> 00:23:17,964
Let's do our best tomorrow as we always do.

566
00:23:17,964 --> 00:23:18,964
Okay.

567
00:23:19,324 --> 00:23:21,594
(A long, exhausting day is drawing to a close.)

568
00:23:21,864 --> 00:23:23,794
- Good night.
- Sleep well.

569
00:23:23,794 --> 00:23:25,204
(They're going to bed to gear up for tomorrow's work.)

570
00:23:25,204 --> 00:23:26,734
- Good night.
- Sleep well.

571
00:23:26,734 --> 00:23:27,774
Sleep well.

572
00:23:29,704 --> 00:23:34,614
(The night deepens as they wonder what memories tomorrow will bring.)

573
00:23:35,574 --> 00:23:37,784
(As the darkness fades,)

574
00:23:37,784 --> 00:23:40,444
(the sun rises over the mountains.)

575
00:23:40,984 --> 00:23:43,384
(Birds stretch their wings.)

576
00:23:43,784 --> 00:23:46,954
(The sound of clear rushing water wakes the morning silence.)

577
00:23:47,484 --> 00:23:51,924
(Just like that, another day begins in Maegye Village.)

578
00:23:54,334 --> 00:23:58,104
(Stretching his arms)

579
00:24:00,534 --> 00:24:02,974
(It's 6:30am. Jin Hee is the first one up.)

580
00:24:04,474 --> 00:24:06,544
(Grabbing his things)

581
00:24:09,274 --> 00:24:14,414
(He quietly leaves the room without waking You Seok.)

582
00:24:14,584 --> 00:24:17,654
(After showering, Jin Hee sits on the veranda.)

583
00:24:17,654 --> 00:24:19,184
(Then he lies down.)

584
00:24:21,124 --> 00:24:27,224
(He's locked in on stretching while lying down.)

585
00:24:27,834 --> 00:24:30,934
(He keeps on stretching.)

586
00:24:31,904 --> 00:24:36,234
(Flailing his arms and legs around)

587
00:24:36,974 --> 00:24:40,644
(Now that he's all stretched out...)

588
00:24:41,714 --> 00:24:43,344
There's absolutely nothing to do here.

589
00:24:43,344 --> 00:24:46,344
(There's absolutely nothing to do here.)

590
00:24:46,784 --> 00:24:49,314
(So, he heads out for a walk around the village.)

591
00:24:51,884 --> 00:24:52,884
(Impressed)

592
00:24:52,884 --> 00:24:54,454
It's a really nice place to live.

593
00:24:56,824 --> 00:25:00,324
(It's a perfect morning for a walk.)

594
00:25:01,664 --> 00:25:05,464
(Clouds linger around the mountain peaks.)

595
00:25:06,204 --> 00:25:09,474
(Maegye Village looks peaceful with lush green rice paddies and fields.)

596
00:25:10,174 --> 00:25:13,874
(The only sound in this quiet village is the rushing water.)

597
00:25:15,974 --> 00:25:17,684
I really like being in quiet places.

598
00:25:20,384 --> 00:25:21,514
I'm the type...

599
00:25:22,214 --> 00:25:24,154
who gains energy from being alone.

600
00:25:25,784 --> 00:25:28,254
(He's the type who recharges through some alone time.)

601
00:25:28,254 --> 00:25:30,724
Have you done the MBTI test?

602
00:25:31,264 --> 00:25:32,594
I'm an ENTJ.

603
00:25:32,924 --> 00:25:35,994
(Surprisingly, he's an extrovert.)

604
00:25:36,364 --> 00:25:38,764
(The extroverted Jin Hee who claims he likes to be alone...)

605
00:25:38,764 --> 00:25:40,264
I thought my body would ache so much today,

606
00:25:40,264 --> 00:25:42,304
but it doesn't hurt as much as I expected.

607
00:25:42,534 --> 00:25:44,704
I worked hard to finish the work quickly.

608
00:25:44,804 --> 00:25:47,344
I feel like I used every single muscle in my body.

609
00:25:47,474 --> 00:25:49,944
The seniors in this village are incredible.

610
00:25:50,174 --> 00:25:52,744
They do such a great job keeping the fields so neat and organized.

611
00:25:53,814 --> 00:25:55,614
(Clapping)

612
00:25:56,554 --> 00:25:57,554
(Clapping)

613
00:25:57,554 --> 00:25:59,984
(He gives off the old-school vibe with his uncle-style clap.)

614
00:26:00,454 --> 00:26:03,254
(This is how Uncle Ji Jin Hee takes a walk in the morning.)

615
00:26:03,894 --> 00:26:06,624
(1. Waking up his system with a healthy clapping routine)

616
00:26:07,094 --> 00:26:08,164
Hello.

617
00:26:08,434 --> 00:26:10,034
You will come over for dinner, right?

618
00:26:10,334 --> 00:26:11,534
I'll see you later.

619
00:26:11,534 --> 00:26:13,064
(2. Talking to seniors)

620
00:26:13,464 --> 00:26:14,834
The red ones...

621
00:26:15,274 --> 00:26:17,804
I think you should eat the darker ones like this.

622
00:26:17,844 --> 00:26:19,374
(Smacking his lips)

623
00:26:20,374 --> 00:26:21,514
(Putting his leg up on the rock)

624
00:26:21,514 --> 00:26:22,674
It's very big.

625
00:26:23,714 --> 00:26:26,644
(If he's curious, he just has to taste it.)

626
00:26:27,514 --> 00:26:28,514
It's sour.

627
00:26:28,814 --> 00:26:29,814
(Chuckling)

628
00:26:30,184 --> 00:26:31,424
I think it's not ripe yet.

629
00:26:33,024 --> 00:26:34,284
This place is really nice.

630
00:26:36,954 --> 00:26:40,824
(3. Taking out his camera when he sees something beautiful)

631
00:26:41,734 --> 00:26:44,834
Oh, this is a wild flower path? I guess that's what it is.

632
00:26:44,834 --> 00:26:46,004
(He spots an information board while walking.)

633
00:26:46,564 --> 00:26:49,034
"As part of the Wild Flower Village Project,"

634
00:26:49,034 --> 00:26:51,644
"we're striving to cover every path in the village with wild flowers..."

635
00:26:51,904 --> 00:26:55,074
No wonder they're well-maintained. The paths looked so beautiful.

636
00:26:55,544 --> 00:26:56,644
"Maegye Village."

637
00:26:56,644 --> 00:26:58,414
"Plum blossom" and "chicken?"

638
00:26:59,584 --> 00:27:01,454
(He makes a dad joke too.)

639
00:27:02,484 --> 00:27:03,784
I wonder if everyone is up now.

640
00:27:03,784 --> 00:27:07,994
(His uncle-style morning walk around the village is almost over.)

641
00:27:08,594 --> 00:27:11,694
(Meanwhile, the girls' room)

642
00:27:12,264 --> 00:27:14,024
My entire body is aching.

643
00:27:15,064 --> 00:27:16,894
I feel like I got beaten up.

644
00:27:17,434 --> 00:27:19,134
Who hit my dear Yoon Seo?

645
00:27:19,534 --> 00:27:20,564
Exactly.

646
00:27:20,864 --> 00:27:21,874
(Screaming)

647
00:27:21,874 --> 00:27:26,274
(The culprit is yesterday's eel work.)

648
00:27:27,204 --> 00:27:29,414
Did you see the people who beat me up?

649
00:27:29,414 --> 00:27:30,444
I saw them.

650
00:27:31,214 --> 00:27:32,744
- I saw three people.
- Three?

651
00:27:33,344 --> 00:27:34,484
Gosh, those brats.

652
00:27:35,414 --> 00:27:36,654
You should've stopped them.

653
00:27:37,884 --> 00:27:39,954
I was getting beaten up too.

654
00:27:39,954 --> 00:27:42,924
(Laughing)

655
00:27:43,094 --> 00:27:45,094
I couldn't stop them.

656
00:27:47,224 --> 00:27:49,464
(She turns out to be another victim.)

657
00:27:49,464 --> 00:27:51,464
I couldn't stop them.

658
00:27:53,534 --> 00:27:56,534
- I was getting beaten up too.
- You were getting beaten up too.

659
00:27:56,534 --> 00:27:59,104
(I was getting beaten up too.)

660
00:27:59,774 --> 00:28:01,714
(Jung Ah's body is aching too.)

661
00:28:02,014 --> 00:28:03,314
I feel like I have bruises.

662
00:28:03,314 --> 00:28:05,144
(Victims are popping up left and right.)

663
00:28:05,144 --> 00:28:07,084
- I have the worst muscle pain ever.
- Seriously...

664
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:09,584
My whole body...

665
00:28:10,114 --> 00:28:11,184
It hurts so much, right?

666
00:28:11,184 --> 00:28:13,184
- It does, indeed.
- The work was very intense.

667
00:28:13,184 --> 00:28:14,184
That's right.

668
00:28:14,624 --> 00:28:15,854
(Dazed)

669
00:28:15,854 --> 00:28:16,854
By the way, Jung Ah...

670
00:28:17,594 --> 00:28:18,964
Can you please get off the mat?

671
00:28:19,164 --> 00:28:20,864
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

672
00:28:21,234 --> 00:28:22,264
I'm sorry.

673
00:28:22,464 --> 00:28:26,534
(Still, we have to do what we have to do.)

674
00:28:26,534 --> 00:28:28,104
- I'll put it over there.
- No.

675
00:28:28,104 --> 00:28:29,304
(You Seok woke up while they were chatting.)

676
00:28:29,304 --> 00:28:30,934
- Good morning.
- You're all up.

677
00:28:30,934 --> 00:28:32,474
- Good morning, everyone.
- Good morning.

678
00:28:33,874 --> 00:28:35,714
Gosh. Why is my whole body aching?

679
00:28:36,514 --> 00:28:39,384
Me too. I feel like I just got beaten up.

680
00:28:39,714 --> 00:28:40,814
- Really?
- Yes.

681
00:28:41,584 --> 00:28:44,784
(Right then, Jin Hee returns from his walk.)

682
00:28:44,784 --> 00:28:45,854
Are you all up now?

683
00:28:46,084 --> 00:28:47,324
- Good morning, Jin Hee.
- Good morning.

684
00:28:47,324 --> 00:28:49,194
- Good morning.
- Did you sleep well?

685
00:28:49,194 --> 00:28:50,194
Yes, I did.

686
00:28:50,624 --> 00:28:51,994
I woke up at 6:30am.

687
00:28:52,194 --> 00:28:53,294
At 6:30am?

688
00:28:53,294 --> 00:28:55,164
I took a shower and went for a walk.

689
00:28:55,364 --> 00:28:56,734
- Really?
- Yes.

690
00:28:57,064 --> 00:28:58,504
You went for a walk?

691
00:28:58,504 --> 00:29:01,034
I made it past the village hall on my walk.

692
00:29:01,374 --> 00:29:02,474
Really?

693
00:29:03,074 --> 00:29:04,134
Really?

694
00:29:05,204 --> 00:29:07,304
- Is it time to make breakfast?
- Yes.

695
00:29:08,914 --> 00:29:10,144
So the main dish is...

696
00:29:10,544 --> 00:29:11,744
- Gambas?
- Yes.

697
00:29:12,084 --> 00:29:13,814
It's scallop al ajillo.

698
00:29:13,814 --> 00:29:15,114
(Today's breakfast: Scallop gambas)

699
00:29:16,014 --> 00:29:20,684
(Today, they will make gambas with scallop.)

700
00:29:20,684 --> 00:29:23,424
Will it take about 30 minutes to prepare breakfast?

701
00:29:23,794 --> 00:29:25,764
Yes. What are you going to do?

702
00:29:25,764 --> 00:29:27,264
Shall I cut the yakbab and wrap it up?

703
00:29:27,694 --> 00:29:28,764
Will you?

704
00:29:29,494 --> 00:29:31,364
- I have nothing else to do anyway.
- Exactly.

705
00:29:31,664 --> 00:29:33,204
Just show me how to do it.

706
00:29:33,204 --> 00:29:34,774
(Jin Hee will wrap up the yakbab while the others prep breakfast.)

707
00:29:34,774 --> 00:29:36,134
Just show me how to do it.

708
00:29:36,204 --> 00:29:37,874
Jung Ah, should I toast some bread?

709
00:29:37,974 --> 00:29:39,144
Yes, we need to toast some bread too.

710
00:29:39,244 --> 00:29:40,774
Then I'll toast bread.

711
00:29:41,004 --> 00:29:42,844
Jung Ah, what vegetables should I wash?

712
00:29:43,414 --> 00:29:45,544
Which vegetables do you need me to wash?

713
00:29:45,544 --> 00:29:47,244
(They say the darkest place is under the candlestick.)

714
00:29:47,244 --> 00:29:49,814
(The vegetables were right under her nose.)

715
00:29:50,184 --> 00:29:52,554
I don't know exactly what dish we're making.

716
00:29:54,154 --> 00:29:55,194
I don't know.

717
00:29:57,654 --> 00:29:58,724
Is it gambas?

718
00:29:59,364 --> 00:30:01,294
(Rinsing cherry tomatoes)

719
00:30:02,564 --> 00:30:04,564
(She puts a cherry tomato in her mouth.)

720
00:30:05,404 --> 00:30:06,604
The cherry tomato is good.

721
00:30:07,204 --> 00:30:08,704
(Destemming the cherry tomatoes thoroughly)

722
00:30:08,704 --> 00:30:10,174
(Putting the cherry tomatoes in her mouth)

723
00:30:10,474 --> 00:30:12,644
(While she's eating the cherry tomatoes...)

724
00:30:12,644 --> 00:30:14,174
Can you help me move the bricks?

725
00:30:14,814 --> 00:30:16,674
- I'll do it. Don't do it.
- It's okay. Let's do it together.

726
00:30:16,674 --> 00:30:17,844
- Do something else.
- Let's do it together.

727
00:30:17,844 --> 00:30:19,014
Do something else. They're heavy.

728
00:30:19,514 --> 00:30:21,244
- Do something else.
- We can get it done quickly.

729
00:30:21,244 --> 00:30:22,554
Find something else to do. Don't do this.

730
00:30:22,914 --> 00:30:24,084
- I'll do it.
- Don't.

731
00:30:24,084 --> 00:30:25,424
- I'll do it.
- How dare you?

732
00:30:25,554 --> 00:30:26,554
(Making a weird noise)

733
00:30:26,554 --> 00:30:27,784
(Communicating through weird grunts)

734
00:30:27,924 --> 00:30:29,024
- Don't do it.
- No.

735
00:30:29,994 --> 00:30:33,124
(The heartwarming squabble over who gets to do the work)

736
00:30:36,164 --> 00:30:38,164
(Laying down the bricks according to his own plan)

737
00:30:38,164 --> 00:30:39,464
You're doing it weird again.

738
00:30:39,464 --> 00:30:41,064
No, I'm using my artistic sense.

739
00:30:42,374 --> 00:30:43,434
Here you go.

740
00:30:44,134 --> 00:30:46,204
I'll bring you the bricks. You design the layout.

741
00:30:46,404 --> 00:30:47,804
- I should design the layout?
- Yes.

742
00:30:47,804 --> 00:30:49,044
Does this require artistic sense?

743
00:30:49,044 --> 00:30:50,314
Yes, it does. More than anything else.

744
00:30:50,314 --> 00:30:51,314
I feel so pressured.

745
00:30:51,314 --> 00:30:53,344
It's more important than food plating.

746
00:30:53,344 --> 00:30:54,814
(The art major is suddenly in charge of designing the brick stove.)

747
00:30:54,814 --> 00:30:57,014
What should I do? This is the toughest challenge of my life.

748
00:30:57,014 --> 00:30:58,554
(Her pride as an art major is on the line?)

749
00:30:58,954 --> 00:31:01,254
Give it a try. Ignite your passion...

750
00:31:01,254 --> 00:31:02,394
(Brick)

751
00:31:02,394 --> 00:31:03,454
as an artist.

752
00:31:05,564 --> 00:31:06,624
I can bring you all the bricks you need.

753
00:31:06,624 --> 00:31:08,194
(And now she's burning with artistic passion.)

754
00:31:09,064 --> 00:31:11,834
(He provides an endless supply of bricks for the artist.)

755
00:31:13,504 --> 00:31:16,704
(After much deliberation, the brick stove is taking shape.)

756
00:31:17,604 --> 00:31:19,904
Oh, it's big. This is great. It's so pretty.

757
00:31:20,504 --> 00:31:21,574
You did a great job.

758
00:31:21,574 --> 00:31:23,614
(Is this an art major's profound artistic sense?)

759
00:31:24,574 --> 00:31:26,484
(On top of the pretty brick base created by Yoon Seo,)

760
00:31:27,244 --> 00:31:29,814
(he places a burner to complete the brick stove!)

761
00:31:30,384 --> 00:31:33,354
