01:32:58,481 --> 01:32:59,541
- That's done.
- Wait. Look.

2264
01:33:00,341 --> 01:33:01,851
They're all gathered together already.

2265
01:33:03,181 --> 01:33:05,481
(After wrapping up the day's work early,)

2266
01:33:06,281 --> 01:33:07,981
- Some came out early.
- Yes.

2267
01:33:07,981 --> 01:33:11,551
(the villagers are gathered for a workout.)

2268
01:33:11,961 --> 01:33:13,561
- Gosh.
- Goodness.

2269
01:33:13,561 --> 01:33:14,791
Gosh. That's right.

2270
01:33:14,791 --> 01:33:17,031
- Kwang.
- That's right.

2271
01:33:17,031 --> 01:33:18,091
How have you been, Kwang?

2272
01:33:18,091 --> 01:33:21,101
- Look at him greeting us.
- That's right, Kwang.

2273
01:33:22,201 --> 01:33:23,231
Kwang.

2274
01:33:23,231 --> 01:33:25,071
You're so pretty.

2275
01:33:25,841 --> 01:33:26,971
You're adorable.

2276
01:33:27,401 --> 01:33:29,741
Gosh. You're so pretty and cute.

2277
01:33:31,171 --> 01:33:32,641
Goodness. Good afternoon.

2278
01:33:32,641 --> 01:33:33,841
(The older sisters in the meantime...)

2279
01:33:34,211 --> 01:33:36,211
- When you make the announcement, - Hello.

2280
01:33:36,681 --> 01:33:39,381
push this button, and turn this on.

2281
01:33:39,381 --> 01:33:40,421
(The announcement begins after pushing the bell button.)

2282
01:33:40,421 --> 01:33:42,221
They'll focus on the announcement.

2283
01:33:43,921 --> 01:33:45,361
Please turn it on for us, then we'll make the announcement.

2284
01:33:46,461 --> 01:33:49,861
(The village PA mic is on.)

2285
01:33:50,331 --> 01:33:51,491
Good afternoon.

2286
01:33:52,101 --> 01:33:54,731
We're Fresh off the Sea's Yum Jung Ah...

2287
01:33:55,531 --> 01:33:57,001
Good afternoon,

2288
01:33:57,001 --> 01:33:59,101
everyone in the village.

2289
01:33:59,371 --> 01:34:01,001
I'm Kim Sun Young.

2290
01:34:01,001 --> 01:34:03,841
- Next to me is...
- I'm Roh Yoon Seo.

2291
01:34:03,841 --> 01:34:04,911
(The three sisters' first village PA announcement)

2292
01:34:05,211 --> 01:34:07,111
Yes. Today,

2293
01:34:07,111 --> 01:34:10,311
we've prepared a meal for you with care.

2294
01:34:10,851 --> 01:34:12,521
We'd much appreciate it...

2295
01:34:12,621 --> 01:34:14,621
if you come to EAT-together MAEGYE...

2296
01:34:14,621 --> 01:34:17,021
by 5:30pm.

2297
01:34:17,791 --> 01:34:21,061
Come for dinner by 5:30pm.

2298
01:34:22,231 --> 01:34:24,731
It's at 5:30pm.

2299
01:34:24,991 --> 01:34:28,031
Please come...

2300
01:34:28,301 --> 01:34:31,631
and enjoy the dinner.

2301
01:34:31,701 --> 01:34:34,571
- Okay.
- Please come.

2302
01:34:35,441 --> 01:34:38,441
Please come. We've prepared a delicious dinner.

2303
01:34:39,441 --> 01:34:40,641
Bye.

2304
01:34:40,841 --> 01:34:43,211
(Feeling embarrassed after making the announcement)

2305
01:34:44,211 --> 01:34:48,891
(Please come, everyone, and enjoy a warm meal.)

2306
01:34:49,321 --> 01:34:50,691
How much time do we have?

2307
01:34:50,691 --> 01:34:52,591
(Current time: 5pm, 30 minutes before serving)

2308
01:34:53,191 --> 01:34:55,561
Okay. You're doing great.

2309
01:34:55,931 --> 01:34:58,461
- Gosh. They made so many.
- I know.

2310
01:34:59,101 --> 01:35:01,601
(How does well-simmered wild rock seaweed soup taste?)

2311
01:35:01,601 --> 01:35:02,731
(Satisfied)

2312
01:35:03,701 --> 01:35:04,771
It's good.

2313
01:35:04,771 --> 01:35:06,471
(She keeps simmering it so it doesn't cool down.)

2314
01:35:06,901 --> 01:35:09,411
(The wild rock seaweed soup with beef is 95 percent done.)

2315
01:35:10,141 --> 01:35:11,811
It smells like tasty braised ribs.

2316
01:35:12,781 --> 01:35:15,351
(Tasting the meat with the younger siblings)

2317
01:35:15,451 --> 01:35:17,451
- Jung Ah, it's so good.
- Yes? Does it taste good?

2318
01:35:17,451 --> 01:35:19,221
- Yes, it tastes good.
- It's well-seasoned, right?

2319
01:35:19,221 --> 01:35:20,321
(It tastes good.)

2320
01:35:20,821 --> 01:35:22,351
(Jin Hee tries a piece of meat too.)

2321
01:35:22,351 --> 01:35:23,951
Gosh. It's perfect.

2322
01:35:23,951 --> 01:35:24,951
- Does it taste okay?
- Yes.

2323
01:35:25,591 --> 01:35:28,221
Simmer it over low heat. Over very low heat.

2324
01:35:28,221 --> 01:35:30,291
(The braised pork ribs are 95 percent done.)

2325
01:35:30,691 --> 01:35:32,101
What do we have to do now?

2326
01:35:33,031 --> 01:35:34,231
- What?
- Are we done after cooking pasta?

2327
01:35:35,131 --> 01:35:36,801
- We have to make pasta, right?
- Yes.

2328
01:35:37,671 --> 01:35:40,171
- What do we do for pasta?
- Should we cook the noodles?

2329
01:35:40,171 --> 01:35:41,741
Let's bring water to a boil and make pasta.

2330
01:35:42,571 --> 01:35:44,811
(Getting ready to cook pasta noodles)

2331
01:35:45,271 --> 01:35:46,541
(The tomato pasta is 50 percent done.)

2332
01:35:46,541 --> 01:35:47,741
We'll add the noodles later.

2333
01:35:48,181 --> 01:35:50,451
- Did we fluff the rice?
- Please check the rice.

2334
01:35:50,751 --> 01:35:52,281
- Let's fluff the rice.
- Rice...

2335
01:35:52,281 --> 01:35:53,821
- Is the rice cooked?
- Check the rice.

2336
01:35:54,381 --> 01:35:56,151
- It's on Keep Warm now.
- Yes.

2337
01:35:56,151 --> 01:35:57,791
We need to open it to see...

2338
01:35:58,761 --> 01:36:00,821
- What if it isn't cooked?
- No way.

2339
01:36:01,061 --> 01:36:03,891
It must be cooked well.

2340
01:36:04,061 --> 01:36:06,131
I have to remake it right away if it isn't cooked well.

2341
01:36:06,431 --> 01:36:07,701
(Nervous)

2342
01:36:07,701 --> 01:36:09,731
If the rice isn't cooked well, we're in trouble.

2343
01:36:11,501 --> 01:36:13,501
- The rice is... Hold on.
- It's okay, isn't it?

2344
01:36:14,901 --> 01:36:16,471
I'll take some out and fluff the rest.

2345
01:36:17,641 --> 01:36:19,781
What should I do now?

2346
01:36:19,881 --> 01:36:21,741
I want you to oversee everything...

2347
01:36:21,741 --> 01:36:24,211
related to setting up the table while we finish up cooking.

2348
01:36:24,311 --> 01:36:27,181
- We'll serve the food, right?
- Yes.

2349
01:36:28,081 --> 01:36:30,221
Get kkakdugi and others ready.

2350
01:36:32,921 --> 01:36:33,921
Gosh. Kkakdugi looks delicious.

2351
01:36:33,921 --> 01:36:35,321
(Portioning it out for easy serving)

2352
01:36:36,731 --> 01:36:39,301
(She takes as much as she cares for the villagers.)

2353
01:36:40,061 --> 01:36:41,101
I think that's too much.

2354
01:36:41,601 --> 01:36:44,201
You can grab more when you run out of it.

2355
01:36:44,671 --> 01:36:45,671
(She portions out just the right amount.)

2356
01:36:45,671 --> 01:36:47,571
- Should I add a final spoonful?
- Yes.

2357
01:36:48,071 --> 01:36:51,111
- I'll take yakbab out now, Jung Ah.
- Okay.

2358
01:36:51,211 --> 01:36:52,211
Right, Jung Ah?

2359
01:36:52,211 --> 01:36:53,781
- I'll make a pretty circle.
- Okay.

2360
01:36:54,781 --> 01:36:57,381
There are a lot, so you can stack them up.

2361
01:36:57,381 --> 01:36:58,651
(Stacking them up)

2362
01:36:58,981 --> 01:37:01,551
Yes. When you make a big pile, it looks more delicious.

2363
01:37:02,121 --> 01:37:05,221
(Scraping the batter)

2364
01:37:05,491 --> 01:37:07,461
- Amazing work, Jin Hee.
- Good job.

2365
01:37:07,461 --> 01:37:08,591
(The long process of frying jeon finally comes to an end.)

2366
01:37:08,591 --> 01:37:11,961
Gosh. Ms. Roh has set up jeon nicely.

2367
01:37:12,431 --> 01:37:15,261
(Braised ribs, pasta, seaweed soup)

2368
01:37:15,431 --> 01:37:18,371
(They'll set up the rest later.)

2369
01:37:18,841 --> 01:37:20,401
- I'll open the packets, Chef.
- Okay.

2370
01:37:20,401 --> 01:37:21,641
(I'll open the pasta noodle packets, Chef.)

2371
01:37:22,071 --> 01:37:23,241
Are you playing a restaurant game right now?

2372
01:37:23,241 --> 01:37:24,271
(Laughing)

2373
01:37:24,271 --> 01:37:25,341
This isn't a game.

2374
01:37:25,341 --> 01:37:26,941
- We're doing it for real.
- Is it?

2375
01:37:27,581 --> 01:37:30,811
We have a reservation for a group of 40 at 5:30pm, Chef.

2376
01:37:31,181 --> 01:37:33,051
- Please get into it, Chef.
- Should I?

2377
01:37:34,881 --> 01:37:36,421
(Awakened Chef Yum adds the noodles to the water.)

2378
01:37:36,421 --> 01:37:38,621
Are we making the pasta finally?

2379
01:37:39,291 --> 01:37:41,221
We're cooking the pasta noodles now.

2380
01:37:41,861 --> 01:37:42,861
(3 packets)

2381
01:37:44,461 --> 01:37:45,601
(Adding a massive amount...)

2382
01:37:45,601 --> 01:37:46,631
Let's use all of them.

2383
01:37:46,631 --> 01:37:47,861
(of the pasta noodles)

2384
01:37:48,501 --> 01:37:49,531
(Salt)

2385
01:37:50,931 --> 01:37:53,471
Let's cook the noodles for ten minutes.

2386
01:37:54,601 --> 01:37:56,511
- We have time, right?
- Yes.

2387
01:37:56,611 --> 01:37:58,641
We have plenty of time. We're waiting to be on time.

2388
01:37:58,641 --> 01:38:02,411
(Since they have time, they clean up in advance.)

2389
01:38:02,981 --> 01:38:05,881
Hey, you're here. Did you smell the food?

2390
01:38:06,681 --> 01:38:09,421
(The first guest of the EAT-together MAEGYE)

2391
01:38:09,851 --> 01:38:12,161
(Sun Young is enjoying the time with the puppies.)

2392
01:38:12,661 --> 01:38:14,321
The two came running at the smell of the food...

2393
01:38:14,321 --> 01:38:15,991
like students rushing to school.

2394
01:38:16,761 --> 01:38:18,731
(Something smells good here.)

2395
01:38:19,161 --> 01:38:21,401
(Where? I'm coming too.)

2396
01:38:21,901 --> 01:38:24,371
(Some customers are already here before the opening.)

2397
01:38:24,871 --> 01:38:26,901
(Meanwhile, Jung Ah checks the pasta noodles.)

2398
01:38:27,341 --> 01:38:28,371
This is driving me crazy.

2399
01:38:30,211 --> 01:38:33,441
It's hard to cook them. They soak up all the water.

2400
01:38:33,741 --> 01:38:35,981
- Is it over high heat?
- Yes. I cranked up the heat.

2401
01:38:37,111 --> 01:38:39,321
(Serious)

2402
01:38:39,421 --> 01:38:41,721
- We have to boil it for a while.
- They are coming now.

2403
01:38:41,981 --> 01:38:43,791
- What?
- They're starting to gather.

2404
01:38:43,921 --> 01:38:44,921
(Current time: 5:15pm)

2405
01:38:44,921 --> 01:38:47,491
(It's already 15 minutes before serving.)

2406
01:38:47,861 --> 01:38:49,891
(I'm hungry.)

2407
01:38:50,531 --> 01:38:54,431
(The villagers leave their home for the meal.)

2408
01:38:54,601 --> 01:38:56,301
(The Siblings', but the cooking crew is...)

2409
01:38:56,301 --> 01:38:57,831
It's not easy to cook the noodles.

2410
01:38:58,301 --> 01:39:00,841
(The pasta is still undercooked.)

2411
01:39:01,101 --> 01:39:03,971
(Braised ribs and seaweed soup must be set up too.)

2412
01:39:04,611 --> 01:39:06,811
(Chef Yum is deep in thought.)

2413
01:39:06,981 --> 01:39:09,781
You Seok, we need to add more hot water.

2414
01:39:09,781 --> 01:39:11,081
It absorbed a lot of water.

2415
01:39:11,381 --> 01:39:12,521
Let's add a bit more.

2416
01:39:12,521 --> 01:39:15,321
(They decide to tackle the most urgent pasta first.)

2417
01:39:15,751 --> 01:39:18,721
(Cooking fast by adding hot water)

2418
01:39:18,721 --> 01:39:19,961
Could you move that?

2419
01:39:19,961 --> 01:39:20,991
- This...
- Should I move this?

2420
01:39:21,661 --> 01:39:22,791
- Hey.
- Gosh, where should I put it?

2421
01:39:22,791 --> 01:39:23,931
- Put it there.
- Okay.

2422
01:39:23,931 --> 01:39:25,291
Put it down.

2423
01:39:25,291 --> 01:39:26,301
(Wild rock seaweed soup with beef is also ready to be served.)

2424
01:39:26,301 --> 01:39:28,031
I'll finish making the braised ribs.

2425
01:39:29,071 --> 01:39:30,071
(Adding loads of sesame oil and sesame seeds)

2426
01:39:30,071 --> 01:39:31,131
It looks delicious.

2427
01:39:32,641 --> 01:39:33,971
It's seasoned perfectly.

2428
01:39:33,971 --> 01:39:35,501
(The braised ribs are completely ready.)

2429
01:39:38,241 --> 01:39:40,381
Could you put the braised ribs on a plate?

2430
01:39:40,511 --> 01:39:43,151
(Portioning braised ribs begins.)

2431
01:39:43,151 --> 01:39:44,151
What should I do?

2432
01:39:44,151 --> 01:39:45,211
- We should move this.
- Don't touch it. I'll do it.

2433
01:39:45,921 --> 01:39:47,251
- Over there.
- Over here?

2434
01:39:47,951 --> 01:39:48,951
Okay.

2435
01:39:49,421 --> 01:39:50,451
All right.

2436
01:39:50,551 --> 01:39:53,161
(Everything is getting done smoothly.)

2437
01:39:53,421 --> 01:39:55,891
(All that's left is the pasta.)

2438
01:39:56,291 --> 01:39:59,431
(Is the pasta that's been causing trouble finally cooked?)

2439
01:40:00,701 --> 01:40:03,671
(She tries a strand.)

2440
01:40:04,171 --> 01:40:08,401
(How is it?)

2441
01:40:08,571 --> 01:40:10,311
We just need to cook it in the sauce.

2442
01:40:11,241 --> 01:40:12,411
The noodles are cooked.

2443
01:40:12,411 --> 01:40:13,511
- Are they cooked?
- Yes.

2444
01:40:13,511 --> 01:40:14,781
- Then we're good.
- Yes.

2445
01:40:14,781 --> 01:40:16,311
- Right?
- We need to cook it in the sauce.

2446
01:40:16,711 --> 01:40:19,221
(From this point, it's a race against the clock.)

2447
01:40:19,721 --> 01:40:22,951
(Finally pouring the pasta into the sauce)

2448
01:40:23,051 --> 01:40:24,851
- Aren't we done?
- Once pasta is in, we're done.

2449
01:40:25,251 --> 01:40:26,391
This is good.

2450
01:40:26,391 --> 01:40:28,821
(Cooking the pasta longer while mixing with the sauce)

2451
01:40:28,821 --> 01:40:30,961
- I'll serve this much first.
- With the broth.

2452
01:40:30,961 --> 01:40:34,401
(Braised pork ribs are ready to be served.)

2453
01:40:34,961 --> 01:40:35,971
- It's done.
- Got it.

2454
01:40:35,971 --> 01:40:37,771
We're confident now that braised ribs are ready.

2455
01:40:37,931 --> 01:40:39,841
- They can also eat pasta.
- Good.

2456
01:40:39,841 --> 01:40:40,941
This is good.

2457
01:40:41,201 --> 01:40:42,741
I think it's all cooked.

2458
01:40:43,871 --> 01:40:46,141
(Portioning the pasta quickly)

2459
01:40:46,581 --> 01:40:47,981
Gosh, look at the pasta.

2460
01:40:47,981 --> 01:40:49,011
(Pasta is also ready to be served.)

2461
01:40:49,011 --> 01:40:50,751
- It looks delicious.
- We're done.

2462
01:40:51,511 --> 01:40:54,251
(What is the current time?)

2463
01:40:54,721 --> 01:40:57,421
- It's 5:23pm.
- We did it so fast. We're done.

2464
01:40:57,421 --> 01:40:59,261
- We finished setting everything up.
- I want to taste it.

2465
01:40:59,261 --> 01:41:00,291
(They're ready 7 minutes before serving.)

2466
01:41:01,091 --> 01:41:02,531
They can come now.

2467
01:41:02,831 --> 01:41:04,891
- I feel so proud.
- I was scared.

2468
01:41:05,661 --> 01:41:06,901
(We made it.)

2469
01:41:06,901 --> 01:41:07,961
You Seok.

2470
01:41:09,071 --> 01:41:10,971
Well done. You did a good job.

2471
01:41:11,431 --> 01:41:13,971
- Suddenly, I feel proud.
- It looks beautiful.

2472
01:41:14,041 --> 01:41:15,041
- We did it!
- We're ready now.

2473
01:41:15,441 --> 01:41:18,771
(Savory braised pork ribs made with love)

2474
01:41:19,211 --> 01:41:22,551
(Pasta in tangy tomato sauce)

2475
01:41:23,281 --> 01:41:26,321
(Crispy and moist zucchini jeon)

2476
01:41:26,881 --> 01:41:29,521
(Kkakdugi, the best side dish with rice)

2477
01:41:30,091 --> 01:41:33,591
(Seaweed soup made with wild rock seaweed the siblings harvested)

2478
01:41:34,321 --> 01:41:36,991
(Yakbab that elders would love)

2479
01:41:37,461 --> 01:41:39,931
(There's even watermelon as a refreshing dessert.)

2480
01:41:40,831 --> 01:41:44,601
(A meal prepared by the siblings for the elders)

2481
01:41:45,101 --> 01:41:46,141
(We're ready to receive the guests.)

2482
01:41:46,141 --> 01:41:47,441
We're ready to receive the guests.

2483
01:41:47,801 --> 01:41:50,071
(The siblings standing at the serving station)

2484
01:41:50,241 --> 01:41:51,841
- I feel nervous.
- Why do I feel nervous?

2485
01:41:51,841 --> 01:41:53,441
Since the guests aren't here yet,

2486
01:41:53,441 --> 01:41:55,041
- I'm waiting for them.
- Okay.

2487
01:41:55,951 --> 01:41:57,851
I feel nervous.

2488
01:41:58,181 --> 01:42:00,421
Why aren't they here yet?

2489
01:42:00,751 --> 01:42:01,921
They're coming...

2490
01:42:02,391 --> 01:42:04,021
- while holding hands.
- Really?

2491
01:42:04,921 --> 01:42:06,421
We're on our way.

2492
01:42:06,421 --> 01:42:07,661
(The seniors arrive together.)

2493
01:42:07,991 --> 01:42:10,031
(Anticipating)

2494
01:42:10,831 --> 01:42:13,161
(The first guests are entering.)

2495
01:42:14,331 --> 01:42:15,771
- Oh, my.
- It's starting now.

2496
01:42:15,771 --> 01:42:17,031
(We're number 1.)

2497
01:42:18,201 --> 01:42:20,241
- Welcome.
- Hello.

2498
01:42:20,241 --> 01:42:22,711
- Hello.
- Hello.

2499
01:42:23,271 --> 01:42:26,281
- Hello.
- Hello.

2500
01:42:26,681 --> 01:42:28,681
(Peeking out to welcome the guests)

2501
01:42:28,841 --> 01:42:31,051
(Everyone goes into meerkat mode.)

2502
01:42:31,511 --> 01:42:33,981
(Once the seniors are settled in)

2503
01:42:34,221 --> 01:42:35,951
- Can we serve the seniors?
- Yes.

2504
01:42:35,951 --> 01:42:37,921
- Yes, please come and get food.
- Hello.

2505
01:42:37,921 --> 01:42:38,921
Please help yourselves.

2506
01:42:38,921 --> 01:42:40,521
Take your time. Enjoy your food.

2507
01:42:40,521 --> 01:42:41,521
(The serving officially starts.)

2508
01:42:41,821 --> 01:42:43,861
I've been fasting since yesterday to enjoy this meal.

2509
01:42:44,331 --> 01:42:46,201
- My goodness.
