It was touching to see everyone enjoy the food.

2760
01:51:45,731 --> 01:51:46,741
I agree.

2761
01:51:46,741 --> 01:51:47,941
But it feels strange too.

2762
01:51:47,941 --> 01:51:50,111
How shall I put this?

2763
01:51:50,911 --> 01:51:53,281
- It's hard to describe.
- I can't put it into words.

2764
01:51:53,281 --> 01:51:55,081
(An indescribable feeling)

2765
01:51:55,081 --> 01:51:56,851
- I almost teared up...
- Me too.

2766
01:51:56,851 --> 01:51:58,911
when everyone kept thanking us.

2767
01:51:59,011 --> 01:52:01,051
I don't usually get emotional like that.

2768
01:52:01,051 --> 01:52:03,251
So it wasn't my menopause that made me emotional?

2769
01:52:03,251 --> 01:52:04,351
- I got emotional too.
- It was okay to get emotional.

2770
01:52:04,351 --> 01:52:05,591
When everyone clapped for us...

2771
01:52:05,591 --> 01:52:07,221
Right, when everyone clapped for us.

2772
01:52:07,221 --> 01:52:08,661
Everyone else...

2773
01:52:08,721 --> 01:52:09,861
- They looked completely fine.
- Right.

2774
01:52:09,861 --> 01:52:12,561
I thought, "I'm just going through menopause."

2775
01:52:12,861 --> 01:52:15,161
I pretended not to get emotional.

2776
01:52:15,161 --> 01:52:16,261
We were all feeling the same.

2777
01:52:16,261 --> 01:52:18,531
I thought that I was getting overly emotional.

2778
01:52:18,531 --> 01:52:20,741
So it wasn't just menopause after all.

2779
01:52:20,941 --> 01:52:23,141
I was so happy to see them enjoy the food.

2780
01:52:23,141 --> 01:52:24,241
Seriously.

2781
01:52:24,711 --> 01:52:26,441
- The jeon was an excellent choice.
- Seriously.

2782
01:52:26,441 --> 01:52:28,181
- Jeon and kkakdugi...
- They were the most popular.

2783
01:52:28,181 --> 01:52:29,681
They also liked yakbab very much.

2784
01:52:30,311 --> 01:52:35,951
(The siblings finally enjoy the food without worrying.)

2785
01:52:36,351 --> 01:52:37,351
Isn't the meat good?

2786
01:52:37,351 --> 01:52:39,351
Didn't the seasoning get all the way inside?

2787
01:52:42,421 --> 01:52:44,431
I have to pack some kkakdugi. It's very delicious.

2788
01:52:44,431 --> 01:52:46,461
- Everyone should take some home.
- Seriously.

2789
01:52:46,461 --> 01:52:47,531
(We made it ourselves, and it's really good.)

2790
01:52:47,531 --> 01:52:48,561
Equally.

2791
01:52:48,561 --> 01:52:49,831
- Hello.
- Hello.

2792
01:52:49,831 --> 01:52:50,831
My gosh.

2793
01:52:50,931 --> 01:52:53,541
- Yes?
- You cooked a meal for us.

2794
01:52:54,041 --> 01:52:55,441
- What did you bring?
- It's nothing big.

2795
01:52:55,441 --> 01:52:57,811
It's ripened kimchi made by...

2796
01:52:57,811 --> 01:52:59,141
women in the village.

2797
01:53:01,241 --> 01:53:02,611
By coming to our village,

2798
01:53:03,481 --> 01:53:05,381
you gave these elders...

2799
01:53:05,381 --> 01:53:07,551
an experience that they never had in their lives.

2800
01:53:07,551 --> 01:53:09,251
- Gosh.
- It will be a memory...

2801
01:53:09,251 --> 01:53:10,821
that they will keep for a long time.

2802
01:53:10,821 --> 01:53:11,951
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

2803
01:53:11,951 --> 01:53:13,391
- It'll be the same for us.
- Thank you.

2804
01:53:13,391 --> 01:53:14,991
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

2805
01:53:14,991 --> 01:53:16,091
Thank you.

2806
01:53:16,431 --> 01:53:18,431
- Thank you for the kimchi.
- It's ripened kimchi.

2807
01:53:18,431 --> 01:53:19,901
This is very precious.

2808
01:53:21,231 --> 01:53:22,631
I feel very grateful.

2809
01:53:24,271 --> 01:53:26,801
Thank you so much. I enjoyed the meal.

2810
01:53:27,841 --> 01:53:29,501
As I've lived for a long time,

2811
01:53:29,501 --> 01:53:30,841
I got something so precious.

2812
01:53:31,611 --> 01:53:32,641
I feel happy.

2813
01:53:33,811 --> 01:53:36,711
I enjoyed the food. Come back soon.

2814
01:53:38,081 --> 01:53:40,081
- Shall we go?
- Let's go.

2815
01:53:40,081 --> 01:53:41,151
(It's time for the siblings to return home.)

2816
01:53:42,851 --> 01:53:44,121
- Three days flew by.
- It's over.

2817
01:53:44,851 --> 01:53:46,151
You look so happy.

2818
01:53:46,151 --> 01:53:47,161
- Right?
- Yes.

2819
01:53:47,161 --> 01:53:48,361
I feel like I can fly away.

2820
01:53:49,831 --> 01:53:51,291
We came here on the first day.

2821
01:53:51,291 --> 01:53:52,831
- It's hard to believe.
- It feels like I dreamed it.

2822
01:53:52,831 --> 01:53:54,001
It feels like a dream.

2823
01:53:54,001 --> 01:53:55,461
(It's time to say goodbye to Maegye Village.)

2824
01:53:55,461 --> 01:53:57,171
This place will be unforgettable.

2825
01:53:58,901 --> 01:54:00,071
I feel like we dreamed it all.

2826
01:54:00,071 --> 01:54:02,101
It was like stepping into a storybook.

2827
01:54:02,341 --> 01:54:03,411
- Right?
- Yes.

2828
01:54:03,411 --> 01:54:05,741
After cooking a meal for all the village elders,

2829
01:54:05,741 --> 01:54:07,181
we went home happily...

2830
01:54:07,181 --> 01:54:09,111
- ever after.
- Ever after.

2831
01:54:09,111 --> 01:54:10,181
Just like that.

2832
01:54:11,438 --> 01:54:12,798
(Is this your first time seeing an entrance like this?)

2833
01:54:13,368 --> 01:54:15,408
(Yeosu, paradise for the siblings)

2834
01:54:16,038 --> 01:54:17,978
(An unusual man makes his entrance.)

2835
01:54:18,908 --> 01:54:20,708
(My charm?)

2836
01:54:21,178 --> 01:54:22,178
(My nose is big.)

2837
01:54:22,678 --> 01:54:24,578
(Who is the guest with a big nose?)

2838
01:54:25,148 --> 01:54:27,518
(Jeong Sang Hun is here, a game-changer at the siblings.)

2839
01:54:28,748 --> 01:54:31,988
(But the sweetness in paradise doesn't last long.)

2840
01:54:32,458 --> 01:54:35,388
(The singles continue their search for love in the spicy inferno.)

2841
01:54:35,628 --> 01:54:36,928
(Warning: Things are about to get spicy.)

2842
01:54:37,198 --> 01:54:39,198
(A barrage of flirting as hot as the weather)

2843
01:54:39,998 --> 01:54:41,768
(What will be their final choice?)

2844
01:54:42,498 --> 01:54:44,998
(Get a grip, this is chili pepper inferno!)

2845
01:54:45,598 --> 01:54:47,238
(I just need one sip of cold water.)

2846
01:54:47,508 --> 01:54:49,138
(The spiciness of Fresh off the Sea will wake you up.)

2847
01:54:49,738 --> 01:54:51,808
Jung Ah passed out.

2848
01:54:51,808 --> 01:54:52,808
(Can it even knock someone off their feet?)

2849
01:54:53,308 --> 01:54:56,078
(The siblings paint a mural in the village for the first time.)

2850
01:54:56,648 --> 01:54:57,778
(Following the art major...)

2851
01:54:57,778 --> 01:54:58,778
(who's putting her skills to work)

2852
01:54:59,378 --> 01:55:04,258
(They add one brushstroke at a time to their memories.)

2853
01:55:05,118 --> 01:55:09,958
(How will the siblings' mural turn out?)
